from ../LanguageData import Hedges, Modals

export abstract anchor Strength as strength:
    description:: string
    rendersAs:: string:: null

export anchor Strengths:
    description:
        A statement can bind firmly, softly, or not at all. The strength of a
        fact records which, so that a requirement is never confused with a
        suggestion. Strength comes from the modal words in @{Modals}, and from
        hedges in @{Hedges}.

    whyPlainStatementsAreRequired:
        A specification describes what should exist. So when it says the
        button is blue, it means the button must be blue, even though the
        sentence never says must. Plain descriptive statements are therefore
        required. This is a rule about specifications, not about English:
        the same sentence in a novel would only be a description.

    strengths: {STRENGTHS}

    example:
        ```text
        The button is blue.              required
        The button must be blue.         required
        The button should be blue.       recommended
        The button may be blue.          permitted
        The button is usually blue.      uncommitted
        ```

export strength Required:
    rendersAs: MUST
    description:
        The statement binds. It is written plainly, or with must, shall, will,
        or cannot. A required fact that is negated renders as MUST NOT.

export strength Recommended:
    rendersAs: SHOULD
    description:
        The statement is advice that can be overridden with good reason. It is
        written with should.

export strength Permitted:
    rendersAs: MAY
    description:
        The statement allows something without requiring it. It is written
        with may, might or could.

export strength Uncommitted:
    rendersAs: null
    description:
        The statement contains a hedge, so it does not say whether it binds.
        An uncommitted fact is never a requirement: it is kept, and an
        ambiguity is recorded asking whether it was meant to bind.

export STRENGTHS:: extends Strength[]:
    - {Required}
    - {Recommended}
    - {Permitted}
    - {Uncommitted}
